# openOODA Native LSP Engine - Editor Setup

File: lsp/docs/LSP_SETUP.oot

Launch: `ooda lsp` over stdio, or `ooda lsp <request-file>` for one-shot tests.
Optional flags: `--stdlib-root <dir>`, `--oodar-root <dir>`, `--compiler <oodac>`.

`--oodar-root` is required for go-to-definition on capability tokens.
It must point at the oodar repo root. The server reads
`${oodar_root}/sec/cap/cap_table.json`. If the flag is set and the file is
missing, the process exits 1. If the flag is absent, builtin definition is null.

## Capabilities

See `CAPABILITIES.oot`. The server implements the methods listed in `CAPABILITIES.oot`.
Engine version: `lsp_facade_version()` (`2.12.0` at this writing).

## Diagnostics

On `didOpen` and `didChange` the server merges `pub fn`, `pub struct`,
`pub enum`, and `pub type` names from every open document into the
completion index (`&CompilerReadCap`), then publishes:

- `E_EM_WEIGHT` (warning) - source exceeds 256 lines
- `E_EM_PINS` (info) - header contains `// Floor:` / `// Thrust:` / `// Patch:`
- oodac `check` errors when `--compiler` or `OODA_COMPILER` is set (on-disk path)

`didClose` clears diagnostics for that URI and drops its symbols. `E_EM_PS` is not emitted.

## Capabilities required

- `&FsReadCap` - stdlib scan and cap_table.json load
- `&CompilerReadCap` - live pub fn/struct/enum/type harvest into the index
- `&ProcessCap` - `oodac check` for compiler diagnostics
- `&EnvCap` - read `OODA_COMPILER` when `--compiler` is omitted

No `&NetCap`. No ambient filesystem. `--oodar-root` and `--stdlib-root` are
the only roots the server will read.

## Proof

From the polyrepo root set `OODA_COMPILER`, `OODA_FS_READDIR`, and
`OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`. Then `oodac run lsp/scripts/test.oo`. That script
emit-c + gcc + runs all 25 qa probes via argv (no `sh -c`). `oodac run`
on a multi-file probe is not the execution path (duplicate TUs). A probe
that prints PASS without an assertion is a defect.
